{"base_rate":0.15246636771300448,"brier":0.0942337817638266,"bss":0.2707513642494036,"bss_hi":0.38719752661964896,"bss_lo":0.12137190588613965,"chart":{"base":[259.7,159.3],"fp":[222.2,196.2],"lead":"62,272.9 272,255.7 482,251.1 692,226.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.27 — higher than 32% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +25pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.9 °C — better than 88% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 5%; promised 67% → rained 53%"},"rel":"74.1,442.5 485.3,235.8"},"country":"NE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.0565321375186846,"ess":337.8484880083432,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Zinder</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Zinder rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (92%), believe about\n<b>67%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 669 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 3.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.27, ranked 91 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(45&ndash;117) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>462</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>13%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>44%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 4 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Zinder</b> <span class=\"muted\">NE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.27</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>45&ndash;117\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>669 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Zinder &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Zinder\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.681948051948055,379.6363636363636 105.23371428571429,304.0 212.1922857142857,184.4 383.2573134328359,28.86567164179104 383.2573134328359,72.3283582089552 212.1922857142857,262.4 105.23371428571429,361.2 58.681948051948055,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"326.50224215246635\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"326.50224215246635\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.681948051948055,374.1212121212121 105.23371428571429,283.2 212.1922857142857,236.4 383.2573134328359,137.52238805970148\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 462 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.681948051948055\" cy=\"374.1212121212121\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 13%&amp;#10;It rained 27% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"105.23371428571429\" cy=\"283.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 44%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"212.1922857142857\" cy=\"236.4\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"383.2573134328359\" cy=\"137.52238805970148\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(15%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Zinder the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.12) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>41%</td><td class='num'>0.063</td><td class='num'>16.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'>0.094</td><td class='num'>3.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>149</td><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'>0.118</td><td class='num'>2.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>170</td><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'>nan</td><td class='num'>0.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":13.80716,"lon":8.9881,"n":669,"n_cities":134,"name":"Zinder","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0019264069264069267,"n":462,"obs":0.021645021645021644,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.13342857142857145,"n":70,"obs":0.2714285714285714,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7340000000000009,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.43557142857142855,"n":70,"obs":0.4,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.7340000000000009,"mean":0.9188059701492538,"n":67,"obs":0.6716417910447762,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.2,"provisional":false,"rank":91,"rank_hi":117.0,"rank_lo":44.95,"reliability":0.008511701409864852,"resolution":0.04670538738995747,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"zinder","station":"","timezone":"Africa/Niamey"}